package mapdemo

// A map whose VALUE is a COUNTED ARRAY (docs/SPEC-TABLES.md §2.8): "A VALUE is
// anything a table field can hold ... `[..N]T`". The value is an ordinary field
// of the generated entry, so its storage is that field's own row, the element
// array beside its `int32` used count (§4.2). Two members are not one
// addressable slot, so the handle every map surface hands back is the ENTRY,
// which reaches both. The element is a TABLE, so an entry's extent walk has a
// nested record to reach.

table Runs
{
    spans map[uint16][..4]Item // [..N]T: the elements and the used count beside them
    after int32
}
